    "background_story": "Amos was a jovial tavern owner in 17th-century England, known far and wide for his exceptional ale and warm hospitality. He was also notorious for being a quaffer, with a penchant for sampling his own brews a bit too enthusiastically. Despite his love of drink, Amos was a shrewd businessman and a master brewer, able to craft ales that drew patrons from all over the countryside. His tavern, 'The Merry Mug', became a beloved gathering place for locals and travelers alike, where Amos would regale them with tales of his adventures and share his latest brews. Though his quaffing habits often left him a bit worse for wear, Amos's good nature and generosity earned him a special place in the hearts of all who knew him.",
